# ROCm environment for the torch SAHI benchmark. Locked with `make lock-rocm`.
#
# lightly-train is installed editable from the local checkout instead of from the git URL
# like requirements/tensorrt.in, so that the benchmark measures the working tree. The path
# is relative to the working directory of `uv pip compile`, which the Makefile always sets
# to inference_benchmarks/, so `..` is the repository root.
-e ..

# The +rocm7.2 local versions only exist on the PyTorch index. Pinned to match the
# pinned-rocm-torch dependency group in ../pyproject.toml.
--extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/rocm7.2
torch==2.13.0+rocm7.2
torchvision==0.28.0+rocm7.2

# No extras and no tensorrt: there is no TensorRT for ROCm, and the torch backend,
# torch.compile, bf16-mixed autocast, SAHI and the latency/mAP plot are all covered by
# lightly-train's base dependencies. onnxruntime in particular has no ROCm wheels.
